From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vaughanb <brenden.vaughan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:40:02 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Read entity states synchronously and resume at each
 state's length

HandleServerEntityStateAtClient re-seeked the reader only after a
handler threw, so a handler that read fewer or more bytes than its state
misread every state after it in the packet. Every kit reader was also
async void, so its read exceptions never reached that catch.

ReadServerEntityState reads one state through its handler and always
leaves the reader at the state's start plus its length, whether the
handler read fewer bytes, more, or threw. The five readers read their
bytes synchronously and hand the apply, which may await a teleport
preparer, to a fire-and-forget method that logs its own exceptions.

Because every state now resumes at its length, a length that is negative
or longer than the rest of the packet stops reading that packet with a
warning: nothing after it can be framed, and a negative length would
seek backwards.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
